    {
      "id": "the-third-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneV_14.6/p@192173",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "RICHARD.\nWhat, will the aspiring blood of Lancaster\nSink in the ground? I thought it would have mounted.\nSee how my sword weeps for the poor King’s death.\nO, may such purple tears be always shed\nFrom those that wish the downfall of our house!\nIf any spark of life be yet remaining,\nDown, down to hell; and say I sent thee thither—",
